course: dictionary
lesson: 2226
title: Many meanings of cover
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word cover has several meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one is right. Ask yourself what is being covered, and why. «Much of Earth's fresh water is frozen in ice sheets, huge sheets of ice covering land» means lying over the land, like a blanket over a bed.
explain: Cover can also mean travel a distance, or be enough for something. «A 4-digit PIN has 10,000 possible codes, so covering the keypad keeps it secret» means putting something over the keypad to hide it. A runner who will cover ten kilometres will travel that far. Money that covers the cost of a book is enough to pay for it.
explain: Cover can be a noun too: a cover is the thing that goes on top, like a lid, a blanket or a book cover. To take cover is to hide somewhere safe, for example from a storm. Check your choice by putting your meaning in place of cover and reading the sentence again.
fact: Cover (verb) means to put something over another thing to hide or protect it.
fact: A cover (noun) is what goes over or on top, like a lid, a blanket or a book cover.
fact: To cover a distance means to travel it, and to cover the cost means there is enough money to pay for it.
fact: To take cover means to hide somewhere safe.
fact: «Edvard Munch... said the figure hears a scream passing through nature and covers its ears» means the figure puts its hands over its ears.
exercise: «A 4-digit PIN has 10,000 possible codes, so covering the keypad keeps it secret.» In this sentence, what does covering the keypad do? | It makes the keypad louder | It moves the keypad across the table | *It keeps it secret by hiding it | It counts the codes on the keypad
exercise: «Huge sheets of ice covering land» What does covering mean here? | *Lying over the land | Travelling across the land | Paying for the land | Cooking on the land
exercise: A runner says, «I will cover ten kilometres before lunch.» What does cover mean? | To pay for | To wrap up tightly | To hide from others | *To travel a distance
test: «Edvard Munch's figure covers its ears.» What does covers mean here? | Listens closely to the sound | Paints over the ears | *Puts something over, to shield its ears | Shouts loudly at the ears
test: «The money covers the cost of the book.» What does covers mean here? | It is lost on the way home | It is hidden under the bed | It is given away for free | *It is enough to pay for the book
exam: «Venus's surface is probably covered over by fresh lava» What does covered over mean? | Made into a crater | *Hidden under a layer | Cooled quickly by the sun | Lit up brightly from above
